# Enable Dual-Lane Mining with Unified Push and Permissive Legacy Support

## Architecture Goal

**Legacy Tritium Lane (Port 8323) - PERMISSIVE:**
- ✅ Accept 8-bit opcodes (0x00-0xFF)
- ✅ Accept 16-bit mirror opcodes (0xD000-0xD0FF) via firewall catch
- ✅ Accept 12-byte payloads (NEW_ROUND/OLD_ROUND modern)
- ✅ Accept 16-byte payloads (NEW_ROUND/OLD_ROUND legacy)
- ✅ Use common push notification utility

**Stateless Tritium Lane (Port 9323) - STRICT:**
- ✅ Accept 16-bit opcodes (0xD000-0xD0FF) ONLY
- ✅ Accept 12-byte payloads ONLY (strict modern format)
- ✅ Use common push notification utility

**Shared Infrastructure:**
- ✅ Unified push notification handler (PRIME_BLOCK_AVAILABLE, HASH_BLOCK_AVAILABLE)
- ✅ Common template generation
- ✅ Shared difficulty calculation

## Part 1: Unified Push Notification Utility

**File:** `src/LLP/push_notification.h` (new)

```cpp
namespace LLP {

class UnifiedPushNotificationHandler {
public:
    /**
     * Send push notification on ANY lane (legacy or stateless)
     * Automatically selects correct opcode based on lane
     */
    static void NotifyBlockAvailable(
        StatelessMinerConnection* pConnection,
        uint32_t nChannel,
        uint32_t nUnifiedHeight,
        uint32_t nChannelHeight,
        uint32_t nDifficulty)
    {
        ProtocolLane lane = pConnection->GetProtocolLane();

        // Build 12-byte payload (same for both lanes)
        std::vector<uint8_t> vPayload(12);
        std::copy_n(reinterpret_cast<uint8_t*>(&nUnifiedHeight), 4, vPayload.begin());
        std::copy_n(reinterpret_cast<uint8_t*>(&nChannelHeight), 4, vPayload.begin() + 4);
        std::copy_n(reinterpret_cast<uint8_t*>(&nDifficulty), 4, vPayload.begin() + 8);

        // Convert to big-endian
        std::reverse(vPayload.begin(), vPayload.begin() + 4);
        std::reverse(vPayload.begin() + 4, vPayload.begin() + 8);
        std::reverse(vPayload.begin() + 8, vPayload.begin() + 12);

        // Select opcode based on lane and channel
        uint16_t nOpcode;
        if (nChannel == CHANNEL_PRIME) {
            nOpcode = (lane == ProtocolLane::STATELESS) ?
                StatelessOpcodes::PRIME_BLOCK_AVAILABLE :   // 0xD0D9
                PRIME_BLOCK_AVAILABLE;                      // 0xD9 (217)
        } else {
            nOpcode = (lane == ProtocolLane::STATELESS) ?
                StatelessOpcodes::HASH_BLOCK_AVAILABLE :    // 0xD0DA
                HASH_BLOCK_AVAILABLE;                       // 0xDA (218)
        }

        // Build and send packet (unified format)
        StatelessPacket response(nOpcode);
        response.DATA = vPayload;
        response.LENGTH = 12;
        pConnection->respond(response);

        debug::log(2, FUNCTION, "Push notification sent - Lane: ", 
                   (lane == ProtocolLane::STATELESS) ? "Stateless" : "Legacy",
                   " Channel: ", (nChannel == CHANNEL_PRIME) ? "Prime" : "Hash",
                   " Opcode: 0x", std::hex, nOpcode, std::dec);
    }
};

} // namespace LLP

